  "body": "`go test ./internal/sessions` fails under `TZ=Pacific/Kiritimati` (UTC+14) and passes under `TZ=UTC`. This happens on origin/main 04ed05733 and was run on mote.\n\n```\n$ TZ=Pacific/Kiritimati go test -tags nogui -count=1 -run 'TestAgyGrows$|TestCursor$' ./internal/sessions\n--- FAIL: TestAgyGrows (0.03s)\n    agy_test.go:152: read on: day &{Models:[{name:agy v:{Input:3000 Output:110 CacheRead:1000 ...}}] ...}\n    agy_test.go:152: read whole: day &{Models:[{name:agy ...}] ...}\n--- FAIL: TestCursor (0.05s)\n    cursor_test.go:287: .../store.db counts no day 2026-09-28: [{2026-09-27 ...}]\nFAIL\n```\n\nBoth tests appear to write a fixed date and then read it back by the local day, so in a far zone the call falls on the neighbouring day. LESSONS.md, \"A fixed date in a test is checked against every clock the code reads\", says to hold every clock or write the fixture at a time that lands on one day in every zone.\n\nFound while running the peak-prices change (model-scoped rate windows) in two zones; that change doesn't touch internal/sessions.\n",
